SUMMARY:Fiddler on the Roof in Yiddish
DESCRIPTION:The internationally acclaimed revival of Fiddler on the Roof in Yiddish makes its Canadian debut at Toronto’s historic Elgin Theatre from May 25 to June 7\, 2026. Presented by the Harold Green Jewish Theatre Company and directed by Tony and Academy Award winner Joel Grey\, this celebrated production is performed entirely in Yiddish with English and Russian subtitles\, offering a rare and deeply authentic theatrical experience. \nSet in the Russian shtetl of Anatevka\, the story follows Tevye\, a humble milkman navigating love\, faith\, and family as tradition collides with a changing world. Hailed as a “revelation\,” this award-winning revival returns one of Broadway’s most beloved musicals to its cultural roots\, delivering a powerful\, timely story of identity\, resilience\, and generational change that continues to resonate across cultures. \nTickets range from $36 – $180 (additional fees may apply) and are on sale now via Ticketmaster.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/fiddler-on-the-roof-in-yiddish-2/
LOCATION:The Elgin & Winter Garden Theatres\, The Elgin & Winter Garden Theatres\, 189 Yonge St.\, M5B1M4 Toronto\, Ontario\, Canada\, Toronto\, M5B 1M4
CATEGORIES:Kids & Family,Performing Arts,Theatre & Opera
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/fiddler-on-the-roof-in-yiddish.png
END:VEVENT
